            <ArticleTitle>[Migraine or headache management: a pharmacy survey].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>395-403</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2515/therapie/2009057</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe the characteristics and the management of migraine.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Data on headaches, drug consumption and life habits of 762 patients were collected using questionnaires and pharmacy records.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The migraine attack was characterized by a severe pain for more than 80% of the patients. The frequency was more than 2 attacks a week in 16% of the cases. Eighty four per cent of the patients had triptans and 45% had a long-term migraine treatment. Nonspecific analgesics were prescribed for 55%. The frequency of over-consumption of treatments of migraine attacks was 46%.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The management of migraine still remains inadequate. The pharmacist could contribute to its improvement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
